artup_lock` next to `_refresh_schemas_lock` in both the normal path and the `RuntimeError` branch.\n  - The new `_startup_sequence()` does the table-count precompute for immutable databases and then calls `invoke_startup()`, under the lock.\n  - `app()` no longer has `setup_db`. `AsgiLifespan` now gets `on_startup=[self._startup_sequence]`, and `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` uses the same method.\n- **`datasette/utils/asgi.py`:**\n  - `AsgiLifespan` sends `lifespan.startup.failed` or `lifespan.shutdown.failed` with the exception message, then returns, instead of letting the exception escape.\n  - `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` ignores lifespan scopes. For other scopes it takes a lock, re-checks, runs the hooks, and only then sets `_started`. It needed `import asyncio`.\n- **`datasette/cli.py`:** `serve` now calls `ds._startup_sequence()`, and its comment says it is the same entry point the ASGI wrappers use.", "ttft_ms": 2243, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 42569, "uuid": "9da549fe-5702-43f8-a9ee-40720dce4121", "ttft_stream_ms": 1741, "time_to_request_ms": 53, "first_content_frame_ms": 1741, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
